WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.369
- The fact that there has been

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:07.240 align:start size:97% position:3%
no accountability with regards
to the whole COVID debacle.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the other example
that comes to mind as well

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.378
is there's been no
one held accountable

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:14.547
for the debacle that was the
withdraw from Afghanistan.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:18.018
And I'm sure we could come up
with a shortlist very quickly

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.286
of other major disasters

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:23.390 align:start size:84% position:16%
of zero people being
held accountable.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:88% position:13%
No one was held
accountable for the lies

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:88% position:13%
that they told around
the Hunter Biden laptop.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.963
You know, we could
go down the list

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.298 align:start size:84% position:16%
that goes to the
heart of your point,

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.300
which is so, so important.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.904
We as voters get to hold our
elected leaders accountable

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.372
at the ballot box, right?

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.008 align:start position:0%
That is our primary way of
being able to make our decisions

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:45.678 align:start size:88% position:13%
about who we hire and
fire in those positions.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:49.482
It is up to us to
hold their feet

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:52.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the fire to bring
about that accountability.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.455
(upbeat music)

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:00.927
- I'm Dave Ruben,

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.896
and joining me today is

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
the host of "The
Tulsi Gabbard Show",

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:97% position:3%
a former US congresswoman from
the great state of Hawaii,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.437 align:start size:88% position:13%
and now a former
Democrat, Tulsi Gabbard.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.604
Welcome back to
the Ruben Report.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:12.906
- Nice to see you, my friend.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.107
It's been a little while.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It has been a
little while, Tulsi.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:18.945
This is my first
interview of 2023,

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.346 align:start size:84% position:16%
so you really gotta
bring it today.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.347
I know you're busy.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.782
I'm on it, I am on it.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
- You're doing your
Tucker thing all the time,

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.418
but I know you gotta you
gotta bring it for me.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.586
Can you do that?

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.822 align:start size:84% position:16%
- No, I'll do my
best, I'll do my best.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.056
- Let's start real quick.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.524
I don't wanna belabor the point

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.926
with leaving the Democrat Party,

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.061 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you've obviously
talked about it quite a bit

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.996
and I was kind of
trying to nudge you

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.132
in my own way for a while.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:42.102
Is there anything you wanna
comment on related to that?

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.369
At this point, you left,

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.938
you campaigned with
some Republicans.

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.107 align:start size:81% position:19%
Obviously the wave
didn't happen,

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.508
but we are seeing
sort of wholesale

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.977
changes on both sides right now.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.880
Anything as we start the
year off on that front,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.682
that's on your mind?

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.150
- Yeah, sure.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, as I think
back to when I announced,

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.021
I left the Democratic
Party in October 11th,

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:05.959
and I listed out some very
specific and clear reasons

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:09.095
why I made that decision to
leave the Democratic Party.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.397 align:start size:88% position:13%
What's wrong with
today's Democratic Party

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:14.434 align:start size:97% position:3%
and my decision to become
an independent, and frankly,

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:18.271
the things that we have
seen play out since then

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.440 align:start size:88% position:13%
and are continuing to
play out, unfortunately,

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:24.511 align:start size:84% position:16%
just further highlight
and underline those

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:27.046
very real concerns that I have.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And frankly, since
making that announcement,

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.451
I've heard from a lot of people,

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.320
maybe some people who
are well-known names,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.622
but just also a lot of

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.758 align:start size:88% position:13%
just everyday Americans
who have expressed

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:41.661 align:start size:81% position:19%
how they have felt
or are feeling

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.230
the same frustrations that I am,

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.534
and that they were grateful

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:51.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have somebody actually
voice those in a way

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
that a lot of folks
across the country heard.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.608 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, you know, there's
a lot happening

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.377
as you know very well,
Dave, below the surface.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.379
That doesn't make
it into, you know,

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.748
the big headlines of the
mainstream media at all.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.816
But it really is this
underlying frustration.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.318
And frankly, it's not just

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.786
with the Democratic Party
as we're seeing happen now.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.354 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's with the Republican
Party as well.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:12.158
And frankly, it points to
just the American people,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.895 align:start size:84% position:16%
pissed off, frustrated
and disenfranchised

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:19.299
with those who are
in power. Period.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.833
- What was it like
for you when you,

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.468
because you basically
made the announcement

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.571 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then you started
campaigning with some people.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.972
I mean, when you were
going to these rallies,

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.107
obviously people liked having

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.576
you there and all that stuff,

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.944
but you do have some differences

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.879
with traditional Republicans.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.747
Was there tension
there or, I found-

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:35.682
- There was no tension.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.383
- That people just get over it.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.284
- Yeah.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.552
There was no tension.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.454
And I think it was,
and sometimes those,

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.189
that statement was made, well,

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.457 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're not gonna
agree on everything,

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.260
which we're not,
who actually does,

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
but all of those
candidates that I went

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:52.999
and supported that, none of
that was planned beforehand.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:55.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my phone just started
ringing off the hook,

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.437 align:start size:97% position:3%
coming from different
candidates across the country

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.172
who recognize exactly
what we just talked

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.242 align:start size:88% position:13%
about is that there
are a lot of folks who,

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:05.278
whether they identify
as independent or not,

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:10.283
are independent minded people
and who are maybe struggling,

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.152
especially in those last
weeks before the election

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.922 align:start position:0%
about trying to decide who
they wanna cast their vote for,

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.857 align:start size:88% position:13%
given their
frustrations with people

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.726
in both political parties.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.929 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so that was
where the requests

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:26.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got came from, frankly,
it was Republicans.

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.501
There were, there
were no Democrats,

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.471
I think, who had the courage to,

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.807
even those who I know agree
with my same frustrations

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
and concerns with
the Democratic Party,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.244
didn't have the courage

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:41.714 align:start size:88% position:13%
to step up and actually
say those things.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.183
So the request I got
came from Republicans

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:47.920
across the spectrum of
the Republican Party,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.356 align:start size:97% position:3%
and regardless of
differences on other issues,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.192 align:start size:88% position:13%
ultimately I chose to
go out and support those

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.762 align:start size:84% position:16%
who value freedom
and who are committed

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.830
to the Constitution
and who recognize

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.301
the need for leaders to step up

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.603
and lead and speak the truth,

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.071
whether that is about leaders

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:07.273
in the Democratic Party
or the Republican Party,

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.708
but actually step
up and speak for

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.209
and fight for the
American people.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.478
- Does that seem like sort of

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:15.415
an obvious extension of the way

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:17.984 align:start position:0%
that your campaign when you
were running for president sort

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.852
of ended in that you
were the last one?

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:22.355 align:start size:88% position:13%
Besides Biden, everyone
else cut the deal,

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:23.923
whatever they had to
do to get into the,

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:26.426 align:start size:84% position:16%
what would be the
future administration?

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:28.194
You stuck and fought,

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:30.229 align:start size:97% position:3%
you didn't cut the deals yet
Hillary Clinton literally

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:33.066 align:start size:97% position:3%
claiming you were in
essence a Russian operative,

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.935
so that where you sit today

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:38.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
as an independent
seems fairly obvious.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.206
If you really kind of-

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:41.808
- For anybody who's been
paying attention, right?

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.443
- Yeah.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.677
- Yeah, I mean, I've always been

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.245
an independent minded person,

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.282 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, for as
long as I, you know,

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:51.984 align:start size:84% position:16%
chose to become a
democrat back in 2002

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:56.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I first ran for State
House here in Hawaii,

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:57.890
because at that time I was drawn

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.092
to the Democratic Party,

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.526 align:start size:84% position:16%
because, especially
here in Hawaii,

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:04.263 align:start size:97% position:3%
I saw a party that was really
rooted in inclusiveness,

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:07.367 align:start size:97% position:3%
in civil liberties and
standing up for free speech

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:11.571
and diversity of thought
and the big tent party.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:14.040
And frankly, there
were a lot of voices

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the Democratic Party
that were voices for peace.

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:20.913
That's changed almost
wholesale since then.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.750
But from that point throughout,

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:27.520
as long as I've been in and
out of politics since 2002,

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've always been an
independent minded person,

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.424
always really done my best
to try to make decisions,

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:34.193 align:start size:97% position:3%
policy decisions or
otherwise based on how well,

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.895 align:start size:97% position:3%
what's in the best interest
of the American people,

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.663 align:start size:88% position:13%
what's in the best
interest of the country.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:38.898
- So let me ask you one

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.933
that's actually
purely on policy,

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.902 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I mentioned
to my locals community

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.904
this morning that I was
having you on today,

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:46.806
and basically my
audience loves you.

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:48.040
Even even the people

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.243
that are say more
right than you are,

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.711
they say, okay,

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
well we can have an honest
conversation with her.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:54.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's trying to talk about
this stuff, all good.

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:57.016
The one that keeps
coming up with you

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:59.419 align:start size:84% position:16%
is they still are
afraid you are going

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:01.521
to come after their
guns if you were

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:03.556
to go back into government.

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:06.259 align:start size:88% position:13%
That they see as
somehow the piece of you

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:08.961
that is still a Democrat
or something like that.

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.496
I'm honestly not
even totally sure

00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:13.166
of your policies on all of that.

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:17.003
So I just leave it to you
to answer their question.

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:18.237
- Sure.

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:21.007
I've always supported
the Second Amendment

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:22.775
and the right to bear arms.

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:27.013
What I will say has changed
over the last few years is,

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:29.248
you know, previously I, you
know, growing up in Hawaii,

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:33.119 align:start size:84% position:16%
we have one of the
most restrictive laws,

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:35.555
one of the most states
with restrictive laws

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:38.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the country as it
pertains to gun ownership.

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:41.828 align:start size:88% position:13%
It takes weeks to be
able to go and apply for

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:42.995 align:start size:84% position:16%
and get a permit
and actually be able

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:44.130
to take the firearm that you

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.032
purchased home with you.

00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:49.902
It's a pretty tough
and rigorous process.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:51.904
So I didn't grow up
around, you know,

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:53.940
shooting a lot of guns
and a different culture

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.074
than maybe a lot of folks have

00:07:55.074 --> 00:07:57.143
in other parts of the country.

00:07:58.044 --> 00:08:00.913
And so, as I looked at what

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:05.885 align:start size:84% position:16%
I felt were common
sense policies around,

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:08.120 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, making
sure that we can try

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:11.824
to prevent mass shootings
in schools and so forth,

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:14.060 align:start size:84% position:16%
that was what was
informing my judgment

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:17.330
and my decision making
as a member of Congress.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.433
The thing that has
changed in a very,

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:24.103
very impactful way
for me is seeing

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:27.540
how the danger of this,

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:32.311 align:start size:97% position:3%
of anyone in government
overstepping their boundaries

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:34.947
and violating our rights

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:38.351 align:start size:88% position:13%
and really understanding
in a visceral way

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:41.954
our founder's intent to
put the Second Amendment

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:43.923
in place, was not only to defend

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:46.993
your safety and your family,

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:51.063 align:start size:97% position:3%
protect your family against
those who seek to do you harm,

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:54.033 align:start size:97% position:3%
but also for us as a people,
as a line of defense,

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:56.903 align:start size:97% position:3%
to protect ourselves against
a tyrannical government.

00:08:56.903 --> 00:09:01.340
And when you look at what
has happened since 2020,

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.175
in so many respects,

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:06.913 align:start position:0%
we see more and more
authoritarian leaning decisions

00:09:06.913 --> 00:09:08.648 align:start size:81% position:19%
and intentions
and policies being

00:09:08.648 --> 00:09:12.151 align:start size:84% position:16%
put forward by our own
federal government.

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.819
And you start to see again,

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:15.321 align:start size:88% position:13%
why the Second
Amendment is important.

00:09:15.321 --> 00:09:18.391
That's what I started to
see and better understand.

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:19.859
There were a number of
things that happened.

00:09:19.859 --> 00:09:23.496 align:start size:97% position:3%
There was the Supreme Court
decision that was made

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:27.633
with regard to the New York
concealed carry permit case.

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:30.970
I read, actually
read through a lot

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.005
of the comments and the remarks

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:35.808
that went on throughout that
case, and also the decision.

00:09:35.808 --> 00:09:40.513
And there were some things
there that provided for me

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:44.350 align:start size:88% position:13%
some fundamental
insight and caused me to

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.185 align:start size:97% position:3%
look at the Second Amendment
in a way that frankly

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:47.853
I'd never had, and very simply,

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:51.724
which is the Second Amendment

00:09:51.724 --> 00:09:54.694
must be protected as strongly

00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:57.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
and fiercely as we protect
the First Amendment.

00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:58.998
You don't have to
get a permit to go,

00:09:58.998 --> 00:10:00.466
and I don't have to go
to get a permit to go

00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:02.034 align:start size:88% position:13%
and stand on a street
